%[text]  What can you say about the stability of the closed loop system and what damping ratio’s are achievable for the dominante poles?
%[text] The entire root locus lies in the left-half plane (LHP), therefore the closed-loop system is stable for all K \> 0. 
%[text] For the dominant complex poles, any damping ratio in the range 0.2 ≤ ζ ≤ 1 is achievable; the locus begins near ζ ≈ 0.2 at low gains, curves leftward through increasing damping ratios, and eventually meets the real axis at ζ = 1, meaning the system can be tuned from underdamped all the way to critically damped by appropriate choice of K.
