%[text] **5. Bode Plot Margins, Bandwidth & Digital Control** (20 marks)
%[text] Consider the controller $D(s)=K\\left(s+z\_c\\right)=47.25(s+1.75)$and plant $G(s)=\\frac{1}{s(s+2)(s+4)(s+6)}$ in the closed loop system shown below:
%[text] ![](text:image:9842)
%[text] a) (5 marks) Plot the open loop bode plot for $D(s)G(s)$ using matlab.
% Your code goes here
clear
s = tf('s');

% Define plant and controller
G = 1 / (s*(s+2)*(s+4)*(s+6));
D = 47.25*(s + 1.75);

% Open-loop transfer function
L = D * G;

% a) Bode plot
figure; %[output:390b951a]
bode(L); %[output:390b951a]
grid on; %[output:390b951a]
title('Open-Loop Bode Plot of D(s)G(s)'); %[output:390b951a]
%[text] What is the gain margin $\\texttt{Gm}$ of the system and what is the phase margin $\\texttt{Pm}$ and at what frequencies do they occur of the system and for the above system? 
% Your code goes here
% Gain and phase margins
[Gm_absolute, Pm, Wcm, Wcp] = margin(L);
% Display results
Gm = 20*log10(Gm_absolute);
Gm  % Gain margin (decibles) %[output:8ee91144]

Pm  % Phase margin (degrees) %[output:70a88916]
Wcm % Phase crossover frequency (rad/s) - where gain margin occurs %[output:15635966]
Wcp % Gain crossover frequency (rad/s) - where phase margin occurs %[output:2c3decd8]
%[text] 
%[text] b) (5 marks) Currently the controller is $D(s)=K\\left(s+z\_c\\right)=47.25(s+1.75)$, i.e. the gain $K=47.25$. What is the minimum gain $K^\*$ at which the feedback control system above become Bounded Input Bounded Output (BIBO) unstable?
% Your code goes here
% Minimum gain K* at which system becomes BIBO unstable
% System becomes unstable when K increases by the gain margin factor
Kstar = 47.25 * Gm_absolute %[output:8ee35109]
%[text] 
%[text] For the current controller $D(s)=K\\left(s+z\_c\\right)=47.25(s+1.75)$, how large a time delay (in seconds) could be introduced into the system control loop before the system would become unstable?
% Your code goes here
% Maximum time delay before instability
% Phase margin tells us how much phase loss is tolerable
% A time delay e^(-Ls) adds phase of -L*Wcp radians at crossover frequency
% Instability occurs when phase loss = Pm
% Pm (in radians) = delay * Wcp
delay = (Pm * pi/180) / Wcp %[output:1232f01c]
%[text] c) (5 marks) For the original controller $D(s)=K\\left(s+z\_c\\right)=47.25(s+1.75)$, compute the closed loop transfer function. Find the bandwidth of the closed loop system using Matlab and assign it to the variable $\\texttt{omega\\\_BW}$:
%[text] 
