% Closed-loop transfer function
Gcl_Q5 = feedback(L, 1) %[output:13817716]

% Find bandwidth of closed-loop system
% bandwidth() returns the -3dB frequency
omega_BW = bandwidth(Gcl_Q5) %[output:628971ae]
%[text] Now suppose that we want to use a digital computer to implement the controller. What is the minimum sampling rate in samples/second (i.e. Hz that you would expect the digital controller system to be stable? 
% Your code here
% Minimum sampling rate (Nyquist criterion)
% Sampling rate must be at least 20x bandwidth for stable digital control
% (rule of thumb: fs >= 20 * omega_BW)
fs_min = 20 * omega_BW / (2*pi)  % convert rad/s to Hz (divide by (2*pi)) %[output:3218dac2]
%[text] d) (5 marks) For a sampling rate of 10 Hz compute the complete Zero Order Hold equivalent of $D(s)G(s)$.
% Your code goes here
% d) Zero Order Hold discretization at 10 Hz
